silence-audit --strict is BLIND on mandark for EVERY project, and the cause is in realisateur/bin/silence-audit.sh, not in the scheduler registry. project_repos() reads the path with a literal grep -- repo="$(grep -oP '(?<=PROJECT_REPO_PATH=")[^"]*' "$conf")" -- but scheduler's schedule/*.conf are SHELL and correctly write PROJECT_REPO_PATH="\$HOME/Documents/Projects/<name>". The grep returns the literal string \$HOME/... , [ -d "$repo" ] is false for all 13 registered projects, projects_seen=0, and the script reports 'BLIND -- parsed ZERO registered projects' and exits 3. Verified 2026-08-05 on mandark: 13 confs carry PROJECT_REPO_PATH and every target dir exists. Proof it is the parse and not an empty domain -- ecosim/bin/silence-audit.sh SOURCES the conf instead (its line 155: repo="$(unset PROJECT_REPO_PATH; . "$conf"; echo "${PROJECT_REPO_PATH:-}")") and reads the same registry fine: 'audited 182 mechanism(s); 70 FLAG(s)', exit 1. Fix is to source rather than grep, matching ecosim's copy. Impact: silence-audit --strict is a build-discipline checklist row in ~19 registered projects' CLAUDE.md, so every one of them is gating on a check that can only return BLIND -- the exact null-discrimination defect the script exists to detect, committed by the detector. senechal has muted that checklist row in its own CLAUDE.md for now (senechal/MUTED-CHECKS.md) rather than fix another project's script. Filed by senechal 2026-08-05, Zach-directed.
